summability: per-site norm sum L^-p finite for p>1; pattern 2nd-moment sum (B2; mu2(m_L)~L^3, one class per L) finite iff p>7; support form K2 (L^2 squares contain a site, mu2(support)~L^4) ~ sum L^(10-p) finite iff p>11. Observed k^4 already for p>5: the sufficient conditions are not sharp; p<=5 lowers the power.
Gaussian comparator (T3): omega_TT^2 = J m1 -> z = slope/2 ; p=3 gives z=1 (harmonic, unit <cos>), with a positive k^2 scalar-trace stiffness
